          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life and Education</strong><br>\nEmmanuel Macron was born in Amiens, France, into a family of doctors. He excelled in school and went on to study philosophy, public affairs, and eventually graduated from the École nationale d'administration (ENA), the training ground for French civil servants.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Entry into Politics</strong><br>\nMacron worked as an investment banker, which equipped him with an understanding of the economic sector. He entered politics as an economic advisor and later became the Minister of Economy, Industry, and Digital Affairs under President François Hollande.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Founding \"En Marche!\" and Election</strong><br>\nIn 2016, Macron founded his own political movement, \"En Marche!\" (On the Move), breaking away from traditional party structures. The following year, he won the French presidential election, becoming the youngest president in French history.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
